codex
Reordered the transaction so the new deploy request is created before any pending requests are marked superseded, and the FK now uses the persisted record’s actual ID at [src/app/api/v1/receipts/verify/route.ts#L583](/Users/moltbot/pp-agent-work/factory-idea-032/src/app/api/v1/receipts/verify/route.ts#L583) and [src/app/api/v1/receipts/verify/route.ts#L626](/Users/moltbot/pp-agent-work/factory-idea-032/src/app/api/v1/receipts/verify/route.ts#L626). That is the minimal fix for the Prisma FK violation.

I also tightened the existing regression test at [tests/deploy-gate-verify-request.test.ts#L448](/Users/moltbot/pp-agent-work/factory-idea-032/tests/deploy-gate-verify-request.test.ts#L448) so it now checks both outcomes: the older request is superseded by the newer request’s real ID, and `create` is invoked before `updateMany`.

Verification:
- `npx vitest run tests/deploy-gate-verify-request.test.ts` passed.
- `npx tsc --noEmit` failed, but only due to pre-existing repo-wide TypeScript errors outside this change set, including `permission-protocol-sdk/packages/examples/minimal-agent.ts`, `reference-demo/src/index.ts`, and multiple unrelated API/service files. I did not change those as part of this bug fix.
